Fixes AI-upscaled characters (Holmes, Watson, NPCs) visibly "hovering" over
the overhead/travel map for as long as it stays open, and continuing to
hover over the next room briefly after leaving the map.

Root cause: Screen::_roseTattooHiresSceneSpriteLayer (the AI-upscaled
overlay for the live scene's walking characters/bg-shapes) is only ever
cleared and re-populated by TattooScene::drawAllShapes(), which runs once
per normal room frame. TattooMap::show() has its own completely separate
render loop for the overhead map (it doesn't call drawAllShapes() at all),
so opening the map never clears that layer - whatever characters happened
to be queued into it during the very last room frame before the map opened
stay frozen there, alpha-blended on top of the map composite by
Screen::update() every single frame the map is up. Depends on
rosetattoo-hires-character-object-sprites.patch (which introduces
_roseTattooHiresSceneSpriteLayer/clearRoseTattooHiresSceneSpriteLayer()).

Fix: explicitly wipe the scene-sprite layer in TattooMap::show(), right
alongside the existing clearRoseTattooHiresBackground() call that already
resets the hires background/composite buffers for the map's own larger
canvas. The next room's first drawAllShapes() call after the map closes
naturally repopulates the layer from scratch as usual.

diff --git a/engines/sherlock/tattoo/tattoo_map.cpp b/engines/sherlock/tattoo/tattoo_map.cpp
index d667a235..1af1e29d 100644
--- a/engines/sherlock/tattoo/tattoo_map.cpp
+++ b/engines/sherlock/tattoo/tattoo_map.cpp
@@ -117,6 +117,20 @@ int TattooMap::show() {
 	// its own scene override via Scene::loadScene() ->
 	// loadRoseTattooHiresBackgroundOverride().
 	screen.clearRoseTattooHiresBackground();
 
+	// The AI-upscaled character/object scene-sprite layer (see
+	// Screen::_roseTattooHiresSceneSpriteLayer) is normally re-queued fresh
+	// every frame by TattooScene::drawAllShapes(), but the overhead map has
+	// its own separate render loop below that never calls drawAllShapes(),
+	// so it's never re-cleared or repopulated while the map is open. Left
+	// as-is, whatever characters were queued into it during the very last
+	// room frame before the map was opened (Holmes, Watson, NPCs, etc.)
+	// would stay frozen on top of the map composite for as long as the map
+	// stays up - the "characters hovering over the map" bug. Wipe it here
+	// so the map starts with a blank scene-sprite layer; the next room's
+	// first drawAllShapes() call naturally repopulates it after the map
+	// closes.
+	screen.clearRoseTattooHiresSceneSpriteLayer();
+
 	// Load the map image and draw it to the back buffer
 	ImageFile *map = new ImageFile("map.vgs");
